(6983790, 1053077, 114969, '<td valign="top">Very nice idea Margaret, and elegant result. <br/>Just one little thing: I would perhaps have preferred the doors to be straight on their sides (especially the middle door). I suppose you used the transform/warp tool (or liquify) to adjust the shape of the doors-layer, but the fact they are curved make them look a bit less like usual doors, which breaks a bit the illusion for me. Nitpicking of course, congratulations on the nice finish!</td>', 'Very nice idea Margaret, and elegant result. Just one little thing: I would perhaps have preferred the doors to be straight on their sides (especially the middle door). I suppose you used the transform/warp tool (or liquify) to adjust the shape of the doors-layer, but the fact they are curved make them look a bit less like usual doors, which breaks a bit the illusion for me. Nitpicking of course, congratulations on the nice finish!', '2013-02-22 11:46:02.000000', NULL, 0),
