(6984479, 1053701, 103142, '<td valign="top">You''re the one!!!!<br/> <br/><a href="//www.nytimes.com/2012/12/20/business/arrests-made-in-maple-syrup-theft-from-quebec-warehouse.html?_r=0" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">$18 million worth of maple syrup stolen</a></td>', 'You''re the one!!!! $18 million worth of maple syrup stolen', '2013-02-23 10:40:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(6984657, 1053488, 41337, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by h2:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by jaysonmc:</b></div><hr/><i> It''s a good concept but looks too fake/photoshopped to me. Now granted, I couldn''t even do this is photoshop, so I respect the effort here. I like those birds and the poise of the man. But the boat is the oomph of the image. Giving you a 6, but this is 10 material for the DPC crowd if you master those PS skills. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks for your comment on my entry. However, I don''t understand what your saying; does it mean the boat is too absurd or did I make a bad photoshop job? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I can''t speak for jaysonmc but the main thing that jumps out at me as "fake" is the boat''s impact on the water. There''s no trailing wake left behind. Now granted it''s not a speed boat but there should still be some residual disturbance left behind by the boat. "As is" it looks as if the boat was dropped straight down on to the water.</td>', 'Originally posted by h2: Originally posted by jaysonmc: It''s a good concept but looks too fake/photoshopped to me. Now granted, I couldn''t even do this is photoshop, so I respect the effort here. I like those birds and the poise of the man. But the boat is the oomph of the image. Giving you a 6, but this is 10 material for the DPC crowd if you master those PS skills.   Thanks for your comment on my entry. However, I don''t understand what your saying; does it mean the boat is too absurd or did I make a bad photoshop job?   I can''t speak for jaysonmc but the main thing that jumps out at me as "fake" is the boat''s impact on the water. There''s no trailing wake left behind. Now granted it''s not a speed boat but there should still be some residual disturbance left behind by the boat. "As is" it looks as if the boat was dropped straight down on to the water.', '2013-02-23 15:04:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(6984662, 1053724, 41337, '<td valign="top">Interesting cell animation effect. I like that almost nothing is the correct proportion (the jar covers, the room as it relates to the people, etc). Editing wise, I think you did a better job on yourself than the guy. The way you laid out his body it doesn''t seem like his face should be pressed up against the glass. The back of his head perhaps, but not the front of his face. Then again maybe that just makes it more absurd.</td>', 'Interesting cell animation effect. I like that almost nothing is the correct proportion (the jar covers, the room as it relates to the people, etc). Editing wise, I think you did a better job on yourself than the guy. The way you laid out his body it doesn''t seem like his face should be pressed up against the glass. The back of his head perhaps, but not the front of his face. Then again maybe that just makes it more absurd.', '2013-02-23 15:19:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(6984897, 1053272, 30982, '<td valign="top">This is fascinating and really well done!</td>', 'This is fascinating and really well done!', '2013-02-23 23:32:18.000000', NULL, 0),
