(6985215, 1053488, 41337, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by h2:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by yanko:</b></div><hr/><i> <br/>I can''t speak for jaysonmc</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>You had to try regardless </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Except I didn''t. But nice try removing the major element from that sentence, which proves otherwise. That''s better editing than the photo.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by h2:</b></div><hr/><i> <br/>- but thanks for paraphrasing what Johanna and Lydia already wrote, Captain Obvious!<br/></i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Perhaps. I don''t make a habit of reading other''s comments to formulate my own least of which comments from ribbon winning photos. The only reason I read jaysonmc''s was because I saw your smug avatar in the comments. I''m glad that you now find it all obvious.</td>', 'Originally posted by h2: Originally posted by yanko: I can''t speak for jaysonmc  You had to try regardless   Except I didn''t. But nice try removing the major element from that sentence, which proves otherwise. That''s better editing than the photo. Originally posted by h2: - but thanks for paraphrasing what Johanna and Lydia already wrote, Captain Obvious!  Perhaps. I don''t make a habit of reading other''s comments to formulate my own least of which comments from ribbon winning photos. The only reason I read jaysonmc''s was because I saw your smug avatar in the comments. I''m glad that you now find it all obvious.', '2013-02-24 13:10:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(6985228, 1053665, 30982, '<td valign="top">Ha!  Way cool!!</td>', 'Ha!  Way cool!!', '2013-02-24 13:24:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(6985304, 1053272, 138630, '<td valign="top">You may or may not be aware that this is one of the photos being used in the online "publications" referenced here: <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=1188924" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">DPC forum thread on LBNelert</a> <br/>I noticed it when I was searching for my own. There were so many from DPC that I could not document them all - if you want to have it removed, see posts from LydiaToo and Mike_311 on p. 5 of the forum thread. To locate it more easily, check both blogs and the main newsletter, starting with the dates when this challenge was in voting or shortly thereafter. <br/> <br/>I know you''ve been following the thread but I thought I''d let you know this was still in there an hour ago.</td>', 'You may or may not be aware that this is one of the photos being used in the online "publications" referenced here: DPC forum thread on LBNelert I noticed it when I was searching for my own. There were so many from DPC that I could not document them all - if you want to have it removed, see posts from LydiaToo and Mike_311 on p. 5 of the forum thread. To locate it more easily, check both blogs and the main newsletter, starting with the dates when this challenge was in voting or shortly thereafter.  I know you''ve been following the thread but I thought I''d let you know this was still in there an hour ago.', '2013-02-24 15:13:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(6985871, 1053488, 131871, '<td valign="top">Congrats!! I love the tones of this. Nice work.</td>', 'Congrats!! I love the tones of this. Nice work.', '2013-02-25 10:56:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(6985872, 1053690, 131871, '<td valign="top">Congrats Christophe!! I am very impressed with the stitching together of the two fish photos for the correct DoF, as I know how hard that can be! I absolutely love the colors as well. I also like how the fish almost has a glow to it. I imagine that is from the aquarium lighting, but it really works for this shot as well. Awesome job! :)</td>', 'Congrats Christophe!! I am very impressed with the stitching together of the two fish photos for the correct DoF, as I know how hard that can be! I absolutely love the colors as well. I also like how the fish almost has a glow to it. I imagine that is from the aquarium lighting, but it really works for this shot as well. Awesome job! :)', '2013-02-25 11:00:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(6986250, 1053382, 138630, '<td valign="top">Some of my favorite entries in this challenge were "real" - I quite liked this street shot and agree with you that documentary can be pretty absurd.</td>', 'Some of my favorite entries in this challenge were "real" - I quite liked this street shot and agree with you that documentary can be pretty absurd.', '2013-02-25 22:47:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(6986665, 1053690, 65319, '<td valign="top">Oh...that''s CHEESE?!!!  I confess...my first thought was mango.  The dark lighting bothers me a little bit as I find myself searching for detail usually so precise and meticulously apparent in your work.  Lovely purple fish!</td>', 'Oh...that''s CHEESE?!!!  I confess...my first thought was mango.  The dark lighting bothers me a little bit as I find myself searching for detail usually so precise and meticulously apparent in your work.  Lovely purple fish!', '2013-02-26 20:07:39.000000', NULL, 0),
